---A creative and its classification data.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Creative
---@field html? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.HtmlContent An HTML creative.
---@field impressionTrackingUrls? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList The set of URLs to be called to record an impression.
---@field agencyId? string The agency ID for this creative.
---@field native? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.NativeContent A native creative.
---@field accountId? string The account that this creative belongs to. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field clickThroughUrls? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList The set of destination URLs for the creative.
---@field adTechnologyProviders? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.AdTechnologyProviders Output only. The detected ad technology providers.
---@field dealsStatus? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.CreativeDealsStatusEnum Output only. The top-level deals status of this creative. If disapproved, an entry for 'auctionType=DIRECT_DEALS' (or 'ALL') in serving_restrictions will also exist. Note that this may be nuanced with other contextual restrictions, in which case, it may be preferable to read from serving_restrictions directly. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field attributes? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.CreativeAttributesItemEnumList All attributes for the ads that may be shown from this creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field detectedProductCategories? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.IntegerList Output only. Detected product categories, if any. See the ad-product-categories.txt file in the technical documentation for a list of IDs.
---@field detectedDomains? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList Output only. The detected domains for this creative.
---@field detectedSensitiveCategories? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.IntegerList Output only. Detected sensitive categories, if any. See the ad-sensitive-categories.txt file in the technical documentation for a list of IDs. You should use these IDs along with the excluded-sensitive-category field in the bid request to filter your bids.
---@field detectedAdvertiserIds? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList Output only. Detected advertiser IDs, if any.
---@field restrictedCategories? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.CreativeRestrictedCategoriesItemEnumList All restricted categories for the ads that may be shown from this creative.
---@field version? number Output only. The version of this creative.
---@field corrections? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.CorrectionList Output only. Shows any corrections that were applied to this creative.
---@field video? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.VideoContent A video creative.
---@field advertiserName? string The name of the company being advertised in the creative.
---@field creativeId? string The buyer-defined creative ID of this creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field apiUpdateTime? string Output only. The last update timestamp of the creative through the API.
---@field openAuctionStatus? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.CreativeOpenAuctionStatusEnum Output only. The top-level open auction status of this creative. If disapproved, an entry for 'auctionType = OPEN_AUCTION' (or 'ALL') in serving_restrictions will also exist. Note that this may be nuanced with other contextual restrictions, in which case, it may be preferable to read from serving_restrictions directly. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field detectedLanguages? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList Output only. The detected languages for this creative. The order is arbitrary. The codes are 2 or 5 characters and are documented at https://developers.google.com/adwords/api/docs/appendix/languagecodes.
---@field declaredClickThroughUrls? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList The set of declared destination URLs for the creative.
---@field vendorIds? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.IntegerList All vendor IDs for the ads that may be shown from this creative. See https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/vendors.txt for possible values.
---@field adChoicesDestinationUrl? string The link to AdChoices destination page.
---@field servingRestrictions? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ServingRestrictionList Output only. The granular status of this ad in specific contexts. A context here relates to where something ultimately serves (for example, a physical location, a platform, an HTTPS versus HTTP request, or the type of auction).

