---A deal represents a segment of inventory for displaying ads on. A proposal can contain multiple deals. A deal contains the terms and targeting information that is used for serving.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Deal
---@field webPropertyCode? string The web property code for the seller copied over from the product.
---@field externalDealId? string Output only. The external deal ID assigned to this deal once the deal is finalized. This is the deal ID that shows up in serving/reporting etc.
---@field buyerPrivateData? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PrivateData Buyer private data (hidden from seller).
---@field description? string Description for the deal terms.
---@field createProductRevision? string Optional. Revision number of the product that the deal was created from. If present on create, and the server `product_revision` has advanced since the passed-in `create_product_revision`, an `ABORTED` error will be returned. Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the deal was last updated.
---@field availableEndTime? string Proposed flight end time of the deal. This will generally be stored in a granularity of a second. A value is not required for Private Auction deals or Preferred Deals.
---@field dealTerms? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DealTerms The negotiable terms of the deal.
---@field creativeRestrictions? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.CreativeRestrictions Output only. Restricitions about the creatives associated with the deal (for example, size) This is available for Programmatic Guaranteed/Preferred Deals in Ad Manager.
---@field syndicationProduct? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DealSyndicationProductEnum|string The syndication product associated with the deal. Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field createProductId? string The product ID from which this deal was created. Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time of the deal creation.
---@field programmaticCreativeSource? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DealProgrammaticCreativeSourceEnum|string Output only. Specifies the creative source for programmatic deals. PUBLISHER means creative is provided by seller and ADVERTISER means creative is provided by buyer.
---@field dealId? string Output only. A unique deal ID for the deal (server-assigned).
---@field targetingCriterion? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.TargetingCriteriaList The shared targeting visible to buyers and sellers. Each shared targeting entity is AND'd together.
---@field isSetupComplete? boolean Output only. True, if the buyside inventory setup is complete for this deal.
---@field creativePreApprovalPolicy? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DealCreativePreApprovalPolicyEnum|string Output only. Specifies the creative pre-approval policy.
---@field dealServingMetadata? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DealServingMetadata Output only. Metadata about the serving status of this deal.
---@field creativeSafeFrameCompatibility? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DealCreativeSafeFrameCompatibilityEnum|string Output only. Specifies whether the creative is safeFrame compatible.
---@field sellerContacts? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ContactInformationList Output only. Seller contact information for the deal.
---@field displayName? string The name of the deal.
---@field proposalId? string Output only. ID of the proposal that this deal is part of.
---@field targeting? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.MarketplaceTargeting Output only. Specifies the subset of inventory targeted by the deal.
---@field availableStartTime? string Optional. Proposed flight start time of the deal. This will generally be stored in the granularity of one second since deal serving starts at seconds boundary. Any time specified with more granularity (for example, in milliseconds) will be truncated towards the start of time in seconds.
---@field deliveryControl? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DeliveryControl The set of fields around delivery control that are interesting for a buyer to see but are non-negotiable. These are set by the publisher.

