---The set of metrics that are measured in numbers of impressions, representing how many impressions with the specified dimension values were considered eligible at each stage of the bidding funnel.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ImpressionMetricsRow
---@field availableImpressions? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.MetricValue The number of impressions available to the buyer on Ad Exchange. In some cases this value may be unavailable.
---@field bidRequests? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.MetricValue The number of impressions for which Ad Exchange sent the buyer a bid request.
---@field inventoryMatches? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.MetricValue The number of impressions that match the buyer's inventory pretargeting.
---@field successfulResponses? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.MetricValue The number of impressions for which the buyer successfully sent a response to Ad Exchange.
---@field responsesWithBids? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.MetricValue The number of impressions for which Ad Exchange received a response from the buyer that contained at least one applicable bid.
---@field rowDimensions? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.RowDimensions The values of all dimensions associated with metric values in this row.

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ImpressionMetricsRowList gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ImpressionMetricsRow[]

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.IntegerList number[]

---Represents the size of an ad unit that can be targeted on an ad request. It only applies to Private Auction, AdX Preferred Deals and Auction Packages. This targeting does not apply to Programmatic Guaranteed and Preferred Deals in Ad Manager.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.InventorySizeTargeting
---@field targetedInventorySizes? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.AdSizeList A list of inventory sizes to be included.
---@field excludedInventorySizes? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.AdSizeList A list of inventory sizes to be excluded.

---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ListAccountsClientsInvitationsRequest
---@field pageSize? number Requested page size. Server may return fewer clients than requested. If unspecified, server will pick an appropriate default.
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. Typically, this is the value of ListClientUserInvitationsResponse.nextPageToken returned from the previous call to the clients.invitations.list method.
---@field accountId string Numerical account ID of the client's sponsor buyer. (required)
---@field clientAccountId string Numerical account ID of the client buyer to list invitations for. (required) You must either specify a string representation of a numerical account identifier or the `-` character to list all the invitations for all the clients of a given sponsor buyer.

---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ListAccountsClientsRequest
---@field accountId string Unique numerical account ID of the sponsor buyer to list the clients for.
---@field partnerClientId? string Optional unique identifier (from the standpoint of an Ad Exchange sponsor buyer partner) of the client to return. If specified, at most one client will be returned in the response.
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. Typically, this is the value of ListClientsResponse.nextPageToken returned from the previous call to the accounts.clients.list method.
---@field pageSize? number Requested page size. The server may return fewer clients than requested. If unspecified, the server will pick an appropriate default.

---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ListAccountsClientsUsersRequest
---@field clientAccountId string The account ID of the client buyer to list users for. (required) You must specify either a string representation of a numerical account identifier or the `-` character to list all the client users for all the clients of a given sponsor buyer.
---@field accountId string Numerical account ID of the sponsor buyer of the client to list users for. (required)
---@field pageSize? number Requested page size. The server may return fewer clients than requested. If unspecified, the server will pick an appropriate default.
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. Typically, this is the value of ListClientUsersResponse.nextPageToken returned from the previous call to the accounts.clients.users.list method.

---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ListAccountsCreativesDealAssociationsRequest
---@field query? string An optional query string to filter deal associations. If no filter is specified, all associations will be returned. Supported queries are: - accountId=*account_id_string* - creativeId=*creative_id_string* - dealsId=*deals_id_string* - dealsStatus:{approved, conditionally_approved, disapproved, not_checked} - openAuctionStatus:{approved, conditionally_approved, disapproved, not_checked} Example: 'dealsId=12345 AND dealsStatus:disapproved'
---@field creativeId string The creative ID to list the associations from. Specify "-" to list all creatives under the above account.
---@field pageSize? number Requested page size. Server may return fewer associations than requested. If unspecified, server will pick an appropriate default.
---@field accountId string The account to list the associations from. Specify "-" to list all creatives the current user has access to.
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. Typically, this is the value of ListDealAssociationsResponse.next_page_token returned from the previous call to 'ListDealAssociations' method.

---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ListAccountsCreativesRequest
---@field accountId string The account to list the creatives from. Specify "-" to list all creatives the current user has access to.
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. Typically, this is the value of ListCreativesResponse.next_page_token returned from the previous call to 'ListCreatives' method.
---@field query? string An optional query string to filter creatives. If no filter is specified, all active creatives will be returned. Supported queries are: - accountId=*account_id_string* - creativeId=*creative_id_string* - dealsStatus: {approved, conditionally_approved, disapproved, not_checked} - openAuctionStatus: {approved, conditionally_approved, disapproved, not_checked} - attribute: {a numeric attribute from the list of attributes} - disapprovalReason: {a reason from DisapprovalReason} Example: 'accountId=12345 AND (dealsStatus:disapproved AND disapprovalReason:unacceptable_content) OR attribute:47'
---@field pageSize? number Requested page size. The server may return fewer creatives than requested (due to timeout constraint) even if more are available through another call. If unspecified, server will pick an appropriate default. Acceptable values are 1 to 1000, inclusive.

