---@field pricingType? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PricePricingTypeEnum|string The pricing type for the deal/product. (default: CPM)

---Used to specify pricing rules for buyers/advertisers. Each PricePerBuyer in a product can become 0 or 1 deals. To check if there is a PricePerBuyer for a particular buyer or buyer/advertiser pair, we look for the most specific matching rule - we first look for a rule matching the buyer and advertiser, next a rule with the buyer but an empty advertiser list, and otherwise look for a matching rule where no buyer is set.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PricePerBuyer
---@field price? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Price The specified price.
---@field buyer? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Buyer The buyer who will pay this price. If unset, all buyers can pay this price (if the advertisers match, and there's no more specific rule matching the buyer).
---@field advertiserIds? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList The list of advertisers for this price when associated with this buyer. If empty, all advertisers with this buyer pay this price.

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PricePerBuyerList gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PricePerBuyer[]

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PricePricingTypeEnum "PRICING_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"COST_PER_MILLE"|"COST_PER_DAY"

---Buyers are allowed to store certain types of private data in a proposal/deal.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PrivateData
---@field referenceId? string A buyer or seller specified reference ID. This can be queried in the list operations (max-length: 1024 unicode code units).

---A product is a segment of inventory that a seller wants to sell. It is associated with certain terms and targeting information which helps the buyer know more about the inventory.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Product
---@field availableStartTime? string Inventory availability dates. The start time will be truncated to seconds during serving. Thus, a field specified as 3:23:34.456 (HH:mm:ss.SSS) will be truncated to 3:23:34 when serving.
---@field createTime? string Creation time.
---@field seller? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Seller Information about the seller that created this product.
---@field publisherProfileId? string An ID which can be used by the Publisher Profile API to get more information about the seller that created this product.
---@field productRevision? string The revision number of the product (auto-assigned by Marketplace).
---@field syndicationProduct? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProductSyndicationProductEnum The syndication product associated with the deal.
---@field hasCreatorSignedOff? boolean If the creator has already signed off on the product, then the buyer can finalize the deal by accepting the product as is. When copying to a proposal, if any of the terms are changed, then auto_finalize is automatically set to false.
---@field terms? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DealTerms The negotiable terms of the deal.
---@field webPropertyCode? string The web-property code for the seller. This needs to be copied as is when adding a new deal to a proposal.
---@field updateTime? string Time of last update.
---@field creatorContacts? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ContactInformationList Optional contact information for the creator of this product.
---@field displayName? string The display name for this product as set by the seller.
---@field targetingCriterion? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.TargetingCriteriaList Targeting that is shared between the buyer and the seller. Each targeting criterion has a specified key and for each key there is a list of inclusion value or exclusion values.
---@field productId? string The unique ID for the product.
---@field availableEndTime? string The proposed end time for the deal. The field will be truncated to the order of seconds during serving.

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProductList gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Product[]

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProductSyndicationProductEnum "SYNDICATION_PRODUCT_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONTENT"|"MOBILE"|"VIDEO"|"GAMES"

---Represents a proposal in the Marketplace. A proposal is the unit of negotiation between a seller and a buyer and contains deals which are served. Note: You can't update, create, or otherwise modify Private Auction deals through the API. Fields are updatable unless noted otherwise.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Proposal
---@field proposalRevision? string Output only. The revision number for the proposal. Each update to the proposal or the deal causes the proposal revision number to auto-increment. The buyer keeps track of the last revision number they know of and pass it in when making an update. If the head revision number on the server has since incremented, then an ABORTED error is returned during the update operation to let the buyer know that a subsequent update was made.
---@field deals? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DealList The deals associated with this proposal. For Private Auction proposals (whose deals have NonGuaranteedAuctionTerms), there will only be one deal.
---@field seller? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Seller Reference to the seller on the proposal. Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field buyerContacts? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ContactInformationList Contact information for the buyer.
---@field buyerPrivateData? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PrivateData Private data for buyer. (hidden from seller).
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the proposal was last revised.
---@field lastUpdaterOrCommentorRole? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalLastUpdaterOrCommentorRoleEnum Output only. The role of the last user that either updated the proposal or left a comment.
---@field displayName? string The name for the proposal.
---@field billedBuyer? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Buyer Output only. Reference to the buyer that will get billed for this proposal.
---@field notes? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.NoteList Output only. The notes associated with this proposal.
---@field sellerContacts? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ContactInformationList Output only. Contact information for the seller.
---@field proposalState? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalProposalStateEnum Output only. The current state of the proposal.
---@field isSetupComplete? boolean Output only. True, if the buyside inventory setup is complete for this proposal.
---@field originatorRole? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalOriginatorRoleEnum Output only. Indicates whether the buyer/seller created the proposal.
---@field proposalId? string Output only. The unique ID of the proposal.
---@field buyer? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Buyer Reference to the buyer on the proposal. Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field privateAuctionId? string Output only. Private auction ID if this proposal is a private auction proposal.
---@field isRenegotiating? boolean Output only. True if the proposal is being renegotiated.
---@field termsAndConditions? string Output only. The terms and conditions set by the publisher for this proposal.

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalLastUpdaterOrCommentorRoleEnum "BUYER_SELLER_ROLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BUYER"|"SELLER"

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalList gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Proposal[]

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalOriginatorRoleEnum "BUYER_SELLER_ROLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BUYER"|"SELLER"

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalProposalStateEnum "PROPOSAL_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PROPOSED"|"BUYER_ACCEPTED"|"SELLER_ACCEPTED"|"CANCELED"|"FINALIZED"

---Represents a publisher profile (https://support.google.com/admanager/answer/6035806) in Marketplace. All fields are read only. All string fields are free-form text entered by the publisher unless noted otherwise.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PublisherProfile
---@field overview? string Overview of the publisher.
---@field publisherProfileId? string Unique ID for publisher profile.
---@field buyerPitchStatement? string Statement explaining what's unique about publisher's business, and why buyers should partner with the publisher.
---@field programmaticDealsContact? string Contact information for programmatic deals. This is free text entered by the publisher and may include information like names, phone numbers and email addresses.
---@field audienceDescription? string Description on the publisher's audience.
---@field domains? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList The list of domains represented in this publisher profile. Empty if this is a parent profile. These are top private domains, meaning that these will not contain a string like "photos.google.co.uk/123", but will instead contain "google.co.uk".
---@field mediaKitUrl? string URL to additional marketing and sales materials.
---@field googlePlusUrl? string URL to publisher's Google+ page.
---@field rateCardInfoUrl? string URL to a publisher rate card.
---@field seller? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Seller Seller of the publisher profile.
---@field isParent? boolean Indicates if this profile is the parent profile of the seller. A parent profile represents all the inventory from the seller, as opposed to child profile that is created to brand a portion of inventory. One seller should have only one parent publisher profile, and can have multiple child profiles. Publisher profiles for the same seller will have same value of field google.ads.adexchange.buyer.v2beta1.PublisherProfile.seller. See https://support.google.com/admanager/answer/6035806 for details.
---@field logoUrl? string A Google public URL to the logo for this publisher profile. The logo is stored as a PNG, JPG, or GIF image.
---@field mobileApps? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PublisherProfileMobileApplicationList The list of apps represented in this publisher profile. Empty if this is a parent profile.
---@field samplePageUrl? string URL to a sample content page.
---@field topHeadlines? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList Up to three key metrics and rankings. Max 100 characters each. For example "#1 Mobile News Site for 20 Straight Months".
---@field displayName? string Name of the publisher profile.
---@field directDealsContact? string Contact information for direct reservation deals. This is free text entered by the publisher and may include information like names, phone numbers and email addresses.

---@alias gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PublisherProfileList gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PublisherProfile[]

