---@field deviceCategoryTargeting? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.CriteriaTargeting IDs of device categories to be included/excluded.

---An interval of time, with an absolute start and end.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.TimeInterval
---@field startTime? string The timestamp marking the start of the range (inclusive) for which data is included.
---@field endTime? string The timestamp marking the end of the range (exclusive) for which data is included.

---Represents a time of day. The date and time zone are either not significant or are specified elsewhere. An API may choose to allow leap seconds. Related types are google.type.Date and `google.protobuf.Timestamp`.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.TimeOfDay
---@field hours? number Hours of a day in 24 hour format. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 23. An API may choose to allow the value "24:00:00" for scenarios like business closing time.
---@field nanos? number Fractions of seconds, in nanoseconds. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 999,999,999.
---@field minutes? number Minutes of an hour. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 59.
---@field seconds? number Seconds of a minute. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 59. An API may allow the value 60 if it allows leap-seconds.

---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.UpdateAccountsClientsRequest
---@field visibleToSeller? boolean Whether the client buyer will be visible to sellers.
---@field partnerClientId? string Optional arbitrary unique identifier of this client buyer from the standpoint of its Ad Exchange sponsor buyer. This field can be used to associate a client buyer with the identifier in the namespace of its sponsor buyer, lookup client buyers by that identifier and verify whether an Ad Exchange counterpart of a given client buyer already exists. If present, must be unique among all the client buyers for its Ad Exchange sponsor buyer.
---@field clientName? string Name used to represent this client to publishers. You may have multiple clients that map to the same entity, but for each client the combination of `clientName` and entity must be unique. You can specify this field as empty. Maximum length of 255 characters is allowed.
---@field role? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ClientRoleEnum|string The role which is assigned to the client buyer. Each role implies a set of permissions granted to the client. Must be one of `CLIENT_DEAL_VIEWER`, `CLIENT_DEAL_NEGOTIATOR` or `CLIENT_DEAL_APPROVER`.
---@field entityId? string Numerical identifier of the client entity. The entity can be an advertiser, a brand, or an agency. This identifier is unique among all the entities with the same type. The value of this field is ignored if the entity type is not provided. A list of all known advertisers with their identifiers is available in the [advertisers.txt](https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/advertisers.txt) file. A list of all known brands with their identifiers is available in the [brands.txt](https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/brands.txt) file. A list of all known agencies with their identifiers is available in the [agencies.txt](https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/agencies.txt) file.
---@field entityType? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ClientEntityTypeEnum|string An optional field for specifying the type of the client entity: `ADVERTISER`, `BRAND`, or `AGENCY`.
---@field status? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ClientStatusEnum|string The status of the client buyer.
---@field entityName? string The name of the entity. This field is automatically fetched based on the type and ID. The value of this field is ignored in create and update operations.
---@field accountId string Unique numerical account ID for the buyer of which the client buyer is a customer; the sponsor buyer to update a client for. (required)
---@field clientAccountId string Unique numerical account ID of the client to update. (required)

---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.UpdateAccountsClientsUsersRequest
---@field email? string User's email address. The value of this field is ignored in an update operation.
---@field status? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ClientUserStatusEnum|string The status of the client user.
---@field accountId string Numerical account ID of the client's sponsor buyer. (required)
---@field userId string Numerical identifier of the user to retrieve. (required)
---@field clientAccountId string Numerical account ID of the client buyer that the user to be retrieved is associated with. (required)

