---@field advertiserName? string The name of the company being advertised in the creative.
---@field apiUpdateTime? string Output only. The last update timestamp of the creative through the API.
---@field openAuctionStatus? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.CreativeOpenAuctionStatusEnum|string Output only. The top-level open auction status of this creative. If disapproved, an entry for 'auctionType = OPEN_AUCTION' (or 'ALL') in serving_restrictions will also exist. Note that this may be nuanced with other contextual restrictions, in which case, it may be preferable to read from serving_restrictions directly. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field detectedLanguages? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList Output only. The detected languages for this creative. The order is arbitrary. The codes are 2 or 5 characters and are documented at https://developers.google.com/adwords/api/docs/appendix/languagecodes.
---@field declaredClickThroughUrls? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList The set of declared destination URLs for the creative.
---@field vendorIds? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.IntegerList All vendor IDs for the ads that may be shown from this creative. See https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/vendors.txt for possible values.
---@field adChoicesDestinationUrl? string The link to AdChoices destination page.
---@field servingRestrictions? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ServingRestrictionList Output only. The granular status of this ad in specific contexts. A context here relates to where something ultimately serves (for example, a physical location, a platform, an HTTPS versus HTTP request, or the type of auction).
---@field creativeId string The buyer-defined creative ID of this creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field accountId string The account that this creative belongs to. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.

---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.UpdateAccountsProposalsRequest
---@field proposalRevision? string Output only. The revision number for the proposal. Each update to the proposal or the deal causes the proposal revision number to auto-increment. The buyer keeps track of the last revision number they know of and pass it in when making an update. If the head revision number on the server has since incremented, then an ABORTED error is returned during the update operation to let the buyer know that a subsequent update was made.
---@field deals? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.DealList The deals associated with this proposal. For Private Auction proposals (whose deals have NonGuaranteedAuctionTerms), there will only be one deal.
---@field seller? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Seller Reference to the seller on the proposal. Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field buyerContacts? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ContactInformationList Contact information for the buyer.
---@field buyerPrivateData? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.PrivateData Private data for buyer. (hidden from seller).
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the proposal was last revised.
---@field lastUpdaterOrCommentorRole? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalLastUpdaterOrCommentorRoleEnum|string Output only. The role of the last user that either updated the proposal or left a comment.
---@field displayName? string The name for the proposal.
---@field billedBuyer? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Buyer Output only. Reference to the buyer that will get billed for this proposal.
---@field notes? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.NoteList Output only. The notes associated with this proposal.
---@field sellerContacts? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ContactInformationList Output only. Contact information for the seller.
---@field proposalState? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalProposalStateEnum|string Output only. The current state of the proposal.
---@field isSetupComplete? boolean Output only. True, if the buyside inventory setup is complete for this proposal.
---@field originatorRole? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.ProposalOriginatorRoleEnum|string Output only. Indicates whether the buyer/seller created the proposal.
---@field buyer? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.Buyer Reference to the buyer on the proposal. Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field privateAuctionId? string Output only. Private auction ID if this proposal is a private auction proposal.
---@field isRenegotiating? boolean Output only. True if the proposal is being renegotiated.
---@field termsAndConditions? string Output only. The terms and conditions set by the publisher for this proposal.
---@field proposalId string The unique ID of the proposal.
---@field accountId string Account ID of the buyer.

---Represents a list of targeted and excluded URLs (for example, google.com). For Private Auction and AdX Preferred Deals, URLs are either included or excluded. For Programmatic Guaranteed and Preferred Deals, this doesn't apply.
---@class gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.UrlTargeting
---@field targetedUrls? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList A list of URLs to be included.
---@field excludedUrls? gcp.adexchangebuyer2_v2beta1.StringList A list of URLs to be excluded.

---Video content for a creative.
